     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Greg,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for the prompt reply. Sure, i&#39;ll file an issue</div><div><br></div><div>I wanted to get the whole brain  &quot;v14 neuropil&quot; by running <span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">catmaid_get_volume(&quot;v14.neuropil&quot;), </span>but it didn&#39;t work. Then i tried running an example in the help file <font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);box-sizing:border-box\">v375</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(38,77,102)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);box-sizing:border-box\">catmaid_get_volume</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(248,248,248);color:rgb(51,51,51)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(21,20,181)\">375</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(248,248,248);color:rgb(51,51,51)\">)</span></font><span style=\"background-color:rgb(248,248,248);color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace\"> </span>which as you said, didn&#39;t seem to exist.</div><div><br></div><div>I just tried  <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">catmaid_get_volume(439) </font>where &quot;439&quot; is the id of v14.neuropil and it worked! So perhaps there is a misinterpretation of the name?</div><div><br></div><div><div>Best,</div><div>arthur</div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
